{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_lots_round_or_opening", "label": "lots_round_or_opening (check constraint)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A BICONDITIONAL, not a disjunction: either a lot has its whole purchasing history (po_id, po_delivery_id, dispatch weight, chef house) or it has none of it. A disjunction would readmit the rejected synthetic-round design \u2014 an opening lot carrying a phantom PO. D01 is untouched: po_delivery_id stays UNIQUE; it never said a lot must have a round."}, {"id": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_balance_close", "label": "opening_balance_close (table)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately NOT a config key: config_settings resolution is dated, so a permanent switch stored there is reopenable by writing a later effective_from and fn_set_config would do it without noticing. `id boolean primary key check (id)` is the single-row idiom \u2014 empty means the window is open, one row means closed, and a second close is a key violation rather than a rule someone must remember. closed_idempotency_key separates a genuine retry (returns the original closed_at, R4) from a deliberate second close (OPENING_ALREADY_CLOSED, TC-29)."}, {"id": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_costs", "label": "opening_costs (table)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "R46 wants a cost per kg on every OPENING row while BR15 forbids the counter seeing a price, so quantity and cost are entered by different people at different times \u2014 an UPDATE, which trg_stock_ledger_append_only refuses. Putting the column on stock_ledger would mean relaxing R1 for one column, a hole in ADR-003. The primary key on ledger_id also makes fn_set_opening_cost idempotent with no key column, and lets the close check for a MISSING ROW by left join instead of a null column."}, {"id": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_fn_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "label": "fn_stock_ledger_opening_closed() (trigger function)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberate duplication of fn_record_opening_balance's check: the function gives a screen a legible Thai error, this trigger makes ADR-021's 'by anyone, ever' true \u2014 including a write function added in 2027 that calls fn_post_ledger directly. BEFORE INSERT FOR EACH ROW because it must read new.movement_type, and the subquery runs only for OPENING rows so the ordinary ledger path pays one enum comparison."}, {"id": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_trg_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "label": "trg_stock_ledger_opening_closed (trigger)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_lots_round_or_opening", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000003_purchasing_production_lots", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_lots_round_or_opening", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000003_purchasing_production_po_deliveries", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_balance_close", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_profiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_costs", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000004_stock_and_branch_daily_stock_ledger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_costs", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_profiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_trg_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_fn_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_trg_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000004_stock_and_branch_daily_stock_ledger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_fn_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_balance_close", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_fn_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260910000011_movement_type_opening_movement_type_opening_value", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_balance_close", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_config_settings", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_costs", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000004_stock_and_branch_daily_product_prices", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_fn_stock_ledger_opening_closed", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000004_stock_and_branch_daily_fn_stock_ledger_append_only", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260910000012_opening_balances.sql", "source_location": null, "we